# The specials are the most demanding thing to compare: they run their own
# command scripts, spawn articles and effects, and (unlike a walk) consume
# randomness. Thunder in particular is a two-part move whose second half is
# spawned by the first.
description: P1 uses all four of Pikachu's specials
align: search
window: 8
ref_lead: -1515
env: MELEE_BOOT_MODE=14
env: MELEE_BOOT_MATCH=13,12,9,0,0
env: MELEE_BOOT_STOCKS=3
# Same menu route as match_move.case, and the same measured relations: Dolphin
# input goes in at port frame + 1515 (dump frames), and the port's match runs
# three frames ahead of the console's.
ignore: mode, scene
ref_shift: 2
run_frames: 420
ref_frames: 2400
trace_frames: 1150
ref_trace_frames: 3100
checks: 250, 320
input: 160: b
input: 220: up*12
input: 224: b
input: 232: neutral
input: 300: down*12
input: 304: b
input: 312: neutral
input: 380: right*12
input: 384: b
input: 392: neutral
ref_input: 236:+START
ref_input: 240:-START
ref_input: 400:+START
ref_input: 404:-START
ref_input: 760:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 768:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 820:+A
ref_input: 824:-A
ref_input: 950:+A
ref_input: 954:-A
ref_input: 1000:P2:+A
ref_input: 1004:P2:-A
ref_input: 1060:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1120:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1130:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1140:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1150:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 1157:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1170:+A
ref_input: 1174:-A
ref_input: 1180:P2:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1240:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1250:P2:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1260:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1270:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 1277:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1290:P2:+A
ref_input: 1294:P2:-A
ref_input: 1340:+START
ref_input: 1344:-START
ref_input: 1420:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1452:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1480:+A
ref_input: 1484:-A
ref_input: 1675:+B
ref_input: 1679:-B
ref_input: 1735:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1739:+B
ref_input: 1743:-B
ref_input: 1747:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1815:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 1819:+B
ref_input: 1823:-B
ref_input: 1827:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1895:MAIN:1.0:0.5
